==============================================================================
1. Corpus section-6 files against the section-4 rule files
==============================================================================
  Rubi section-4 rule files: 57
  Rubi section-6 rule files: 13

  Section 6 HAS a miscellany rule file — 6.7.9 Active hyperbolic
  functions — and this port generates and loads it. So the
  miscellany entries are not deferring for want of a section-6
  file; they defer because 6.7.9 covers a DIFFERENT shape.
  6.7.9 is 96 rules and every LHS carries an (e+f x)^m factor
  over a hyperbolic quotient — the x-CARRYING shapes.

  The section-4 rule files with NO section-6 counterpart are the
  pure-trig-product families — exactly what a hyperbolic
  miscellany integrand with no bare x is:
    4.1 Sine/4.1.0.1 (a sin)^m (b trg)^n.m
    4.1 Sine/4.1.0.2 (a trg)^m (b tan)^n.m
    4.1 Sine/4.1.0.3 (a csc)^m (b sec)^n.m
    4.1 Sine/4.1.5 trig^m (a cos+b sin)^n.m
    4.1 Sine/4.1.6 (a+b cos+c sin)^n.m
    4.1 Sine/4.1.8 trig^m (a+b cos^p+c sin^q)^n.m
    4.7 Miscellaneous/4.7.1 Sine normalization rules.m
    4.7 Miscellaneous/4.7.2 Tangent normalization rules.m
    4.7 Miscellaneous/4.7.3 Secant normalization rules.m
    4.7 Miscellaneous/4.7.4 (c trig)^m (d trig)^n.m
    4.7 Miscellaneous/4.7.5 Inert trig functions.m
    4.7 Miscellaneous/4.7.9 Active trig functions.m

  FINDING (structural, not yet decisive): the shapes the class-6
  miscellany files actually contain — products and sums of
  hyperbolics of a linear argument — have their rules in section
  4 only. Whether the BRIDGE hands them over is measurement 2.

